1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:01,790
Inside an Arctic mountain,

2
00:00:01,790 --> 00:00:04,530
there's a door built for the end of the world

3
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:06,600
and someone has already opened it.

4
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:09,350
This is the Svalbard Global Seed Vault,

5
00:00:09,350 --> 00:00:13,920
on a Norwegian island about thirteen hundred kilometres from the North Pole.

6
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:17,840
A tunnel runs more than a hundred metres into the mountain,

7
00:00:17,840 --> 00:00:20,230
to vaults kept at minus eighteen degrees.

8
00:00:20,700 --> 00:00:23,710
Inside are more than a million seed samples,

9
00:00:23,710 --> 00:00:26,860
from almost every country. Rice, wheat, beans.

10
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:28,230
Backups of our food.

11
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:29,930
If the power fails,

12
00:00:29,930 --> 00:00:32,450
the permafrost should keep them frozen.

13
00:00:32,450 --> 00:00:34,910
And it sits high above the rising sea.

14
00:00:35,400 --> 00:00:36,930
Then, in twenty fifteen,

15
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:40,960
war in Syria cut scientists off from their seed bank in Aleppo.

16
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:42,710
So for the first time,

17
00:00:42,710 --> 00:00:44,790
they withdrew seeds from the vault.

18
00:00:44,790 --> 00:00:45,810
They regrew them,

19
00:00:45,810 --> 00:00:47,710
and later sent fresh seeds back.

20
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:49,350
A doomsday vault

21
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:50,940
that's already been needed.

22
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:52,690
What would you save inside?
